A||N||9||87GTBro||Flying Horse!!!||||1||
Z||000000||87GTBro||02-08-2000||12:26 AM||||Ever stop to think about why the Fiero logo is a flying horse?  I found one reason:<P>Just the other day, I took my new 86 GT out on the highway for the first time since I bought it.  I was taking my girlfriend somewhere (her first time to ride in my new car) and we were having a nice conversation.  I was obeying the speed limit and driving nicely.  You know, I wasn't bothering anybody.<BR>Then, out of the corner of my eye, I see a red car passing me.  Then suspiciously, the driver slowed as he pulled along side me.  I look over to see a 98 mustang driving right beside me and I hear the taunting howl of the engine as the driver initiated a duel.<BR>At first, I ignored the guy, thinking of how immature the guy must be.  Then I remembered my girlfriend was sitting in the passenger seat.  I can't go down without a fight!  The mustang took off before I did.  He had about a 2 second gain on me.  I flipped my 4sp into 3rd and flored it. 3, 4, 5000 RPM, then 4th gear!  I was flyin!!!!  I flew past that annoying red mustang as I exited the highway.<BR>My first race was exhilarating!  I am in love with my new Fiero.  There is just something about it.  Nobody ever challenged me in my old Sunbird!  Now THIS Pontiac is DRIVING EXCITEMENT!<P>But I did figure out why the Fiero logo is a flying horse.  Flying horses are much faster than running horses.  I can't wait to experience my NEXT duel!<P>Anybody have any other exciting stories?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||02-08-2000||02:47 AM||||Nice story  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Do you know if it was a V6 'stang or a V8?  You can tell by the wheels easily; The V6's have those six spoke wheels most of the time.  I think it's hilarious that a 12 year old car can whoops the pants off of a brand new "muscle" car.||||reg||7
Z||000002||87GTBro||02-08-2000||10:58 AM||||I was having too much fun to notice the wheels on the car.  Most likely, it was a V6 just like mine, but I am not exactly sure.||||reg||6
Z||000003||dogtired||02-08-2000||01:47 PM||||Been There!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Done That!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Now you know why elephants don't FLY   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Can you imagine? Horse Apples on the hood of a Mustang?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>GREAT KILL!!<p>[This message has been edited by dogtired (edited 02-08-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||87PegasusGT||02-08-2000||03:54 PM||||It was a V6. My 87Gt Whooped some new V6 Mustwang also, but even with my mods, I can't take the new V8. That will change when I finish my twin turbo 3.4........  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">I should then be able to take a new 'Vette.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||02-08-2000||04:53 PM||||I got killed by Plymouth Horizon or some other boxy Chrystler today.  His car was blue and had a mismatched right fender.  He was driving really fast before the light, but I didn't think he would try me.  He was in left lane, I was in right.  Light turned green and he launched hard (had a stick because I could hear one of his 175/75/R13 tires squeak like a little mouse).  I mashed it in first and then second.  I wasn't getting anywhere by sixty so I just shut it down.  He had a jump on me, but I was hangin' in there.  Those K cars must have a lot of power.  Man that hurt.||||reg||8
Z||000006||william_thorniii||02-08-2000||05:31 PM||||Eric,<P>Must have had a Shelby transplant.  Factory they came in menacing black and had a rather large hood scoop.  They used a turbocharged/intercooled 2.2L if I am not mistaken.  Standard Omni/Horizon's cannot take a 2.8L Fiero without extensive work and or very different skilled drivers.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000007||fiero56||02-08-2000||06:22 PM||||Had a roomate last summer with a '92 Sundance. Even with only 50,000 miles, it was slow and unresponsive. I rode in it once, no tach, but even when he had it floored it took forever to get up to 65, longer than the onramp.<P>Just a side note, while in heavy traffic today, some guy in a Metro was giving me the nod and revving the engine. He knew there was no way we could have gone with that much traffic, was pretty funny though.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 02-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric||02-08-2000||06:40 PM||||My car will run well into the 14s with a skilled driver, but skilled I'm not.  I've never really thought much of drag racing, so I'm not well practiced.  I'm also afraid to take my new engine much over 5k rpm.  I'm considering a turbo so to all those Kcars out there WATCH OUT!  Did have some fun on a little back road though (lots of turns and hills).<P>My sister drives a turbo lebaron and it's very slow even when I'm not the one behind the wheel.  Sometimes I look at the turbo and imagine it in my GT.  She would never know its gone.||||reg||1
Z||000009||wkayl||02-08-2000||10:43 PM||||Be careful out there.  In '75 I had a 71 Challenger R/T.  With a girl in the front seat with me a Mustang nailed it for 2 stop lights in a row.  At the 3rd light the girl said "Your not going to let a Mustang do that to you, are you"?  I smoked him!!  After the cop got done writing me a ticket I asked him why he stopped me and not the Mustang?  He said "He was loosing.  Maybe he won't do it again.  You were winning.  I caught you and now you WON'T do it again, will you". I got very lucky because he wrote the ticket for 10 miles over speed limit.||||reg||1
